  "coverage": [
    "Decoded execution facts carry the archive identity captured during validation, on cache misses and hits. End-to-end repair swaps the archive during fresh live observation, retries once, and retains uncertainty without replaying historical effects.",
    "Provider-only repair reports preparation-time file issues consistently but ignores file churn when publishing its database-only change. Recovery publication performs metadata/path identity checks without reopening or reading archives.",
    "Trusted canonical aliases of configured artifact and capture roots normalize to portable identifiers while subordinate symlinks, foreign ownership, and private archive permission checks remain strict.",
    "Root-aware repair and checkpoint candidate descriptors retain the actual creation path and identity. Cleanup removes unused candidates after stale/deferred failure and after a writer throws following file publication, while preserving existing, referenced, and replaced archives.",
    "Optional token allocation, token-query, infrastructure-query, and cache construction failures leave valid loads successful with empty cache trust; malformed revision tokens and altered infrastructure remain errors. Next save is checked before reload.",
    "Operational provider-row read errors abort repair immediately both with and without automatic transaction rollback. The original failure is retained, no further SQL reads occur, and no backup or repair rows are written.",
    "Fragmented Chat Completions structural errors retain initial or ID/name-bearing frames with empty-body transports and prefer the full HTTP body otherwise. Valid empty argument objects succeed; empty argument strings remain malformed.",
    "Prepared SQL writers share explicit column lists without decoding during repair publication. Archive reads are asserted per Tools instance, and the provider-read test callback has exception-safe scope cleanup plus a consumed assertion.",
    "Existing cancellation, consumer exceptions, transport retry, one-retry contention, private backup diagnostics, legacy recovery, fork/compaction, committed response rollback, and receipt safeguards remain covered.",
    "Interleaved 1 MiB and 9 MiB provider histories retain suffix-only serialization and zero unchanged-row reads across unrelated-session commits. Serialized cache caps and zero ordinary capture scans remain intact."
  ],
  "excluded": [
    "Session-scoped repair versioning",
    "Schema migrations",
    "Relaxed trust checks",
    "Empty-argument compatibility expansion",
    "Live provider requests",
    "Tiger hardware execution",
    "Unrelated catalog/model changes"
  ],
